WEBVTT

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.900
She’s packing for a family visit.

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:03.600
Clothes go in the suitcase.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:04.860
The doorbell rings.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.260
Then she comes back… and loses her place.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:11.800
For someone living with dementia, a small
interruption can

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.260
make a familiar task difficult to pick up
again.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.240
Retracing those steps takes effort, and may

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.840
mean asking someone else for help.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.840
What’s at stake is more than a forgotten
charger.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.980
It’s everyday independence.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.880
Threadline brings her recorded plan and
recent notes back into view.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.820
“What was my next planned step?”

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.000
Her plan and earlier notes give her a place
to restart.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.220
In our prototype, she can review what was

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.700
captured, correct it, and see the source.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.000
Unrecorded progress stays unknown.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.100
That’s the difference: support tied to her
intention and context.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.820
This fictional demo explores a simple goal:
help people

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.940
keep their place, and their say, in everyday
life.
